        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "A thorough examination or checking of documentation, records, processes, or systems to confirm compliance or adherence. An inspection needs to have a defined set of acceptance criteria (e.g. a checklist), a documentation of roles involved in the inspection (e.g. to document the inspector's independence) and a clear documentation of when and how it was performed."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label": [
      {
        "@value": "inspection"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/IsoAutomationLevel",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Defines the level of automation a system possesses."
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Software/contentIdentifier",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "A canonical, unique, immutable identifier of the artifact content, that may be\nused for verifying its identity and/or integrity."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range": [
      {
        "@id": "https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Software/ContentIdentifier"
      }
    ]
  },
